  "description": "SB-2627 B5 \u2014 shared behavioral oracle for the totalInclusion contract. Both webapp (`apps/webapp/utils/shared/quotes/totalInclusion.ts`) and addin (`apps/outlook-addin/src/lib/totalInclusion.ts`) MUST produce identical outputs for every case below. The drift detectors are the two app-side fixture tests \u2014 `apps/webapp/utils/shared/quotes/__tests__/totalInclusion.shared.test.ts` and `apps/outlook-addin/src/lib/__tests__/totalInclusion.test.ts` \u2014 both load this fixture and assert the helper's output. If either copy diverges, the corresponding test fails. Per the W2 inline-mirror helper-home decision; replace with a workspace-package import once `apps/shared-lib/` exists (SB-2649). Truth-table semantics encoded: 3 totalKinds (sell, buy, rollup_buy) x 5 flag classes (clean, removed, invisible, optional, incoterm) + regression cells (double-skip + asymmetry + null-default guards) + the SB-5069 bucket-scope and SB-5834 row-owner axes. MATH vs PRESENTATION (Amendment 9, user-confirmed 2026-05-08): is_visible is a presentation flag, NOT a math flag. Hidden charges (is_visible=false) still CONTRIBUTE to the grand total \u2014 their amount is absorbed into base freight via `qv2HiddenSurcharge.ts`. Therefore the contract does NOT exclude hidden charges; all `invisible_*` non-buy cells return INCLUDED (because the only thing is_visible=false controls is whether the row is rendered as its own line item, which is the consumer's `isHidden()` decision). Per Amendment 5 prose + user 3.1.3 ack: `buy` bypasses all 3 customer-facing math flags (only is_removed excludes) for VENDOR-side rows (`surchargeSource` 'carrier' / 'breakdown' / 'added' (the rate's own vendor accessorials), absent = the legacy DB default 'carrier', or any value added later — an unknown owner stays in cost) — a vendor's is_included_in_total=false is the vendor's own optionality and the vendor may still bill it (SB-4088 / SB-5494). SB-5834 (user-confirmed 2026-10-16): an OPERATOR-side row ('global' / 'manual') marked Optional is not a cost, so `buy` honours its is_included_in_total (cells `optional_buy_*`); `rollup_buy` MIRRORS `sell` semantics (preserves the strict-filter status quo at mapQv2ToUwlFormat.ts:1644 \u2014 rollup buy intentionally diverges from row-level calculateBuyTotal). Per user 3.1.4 ack: `buy` is unified across UWL + addin (single totalKind, not separate addin_buy).",
